# Over 536870912x32768x32768 CTAs of 32 threads, 2^64 threads leave
# i64: the count of the kernel's first block over the launch is
# unknown, and so are the instruction and warp instruction counts, but
# thread 0 of each CTA stores 4 B, 2^61 B in all. micro_lane0_copy's
# thread 0 loads and stores 8 B: 2^62 B each way, whose sum leaves i64
# but is no overflow in its AI.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/lane0_store.ptx --grid 536870912,32768,32768 | FileCheck "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --annotate %fixtures/micro/lane0_store.ptx --grid 536870912,32768,32768 | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
CHECK: totals per launch [static]:
CHECK: instructions = 0 + unknown, warp instructions = 0 + unknown
CHECK: kernel micro_lane0_copy
CHECK: totals per launch [static]:
CHECK: AI(global) = 0 flop/B
ANN: {{^}}.visible .entry micro_lane0_store( // grid 536870912×32768×32768 | block 32×1×1 | per launch: global store 2,305,843,009,213,693,952 B; param load ? B{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	ld.param.u64 	%rd1, [micro_lane0_store_param_0]; // [<block 0>] warp * × lane * | exec ?{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}.visible .entry micro_lane0_copy( // grid 536870912×32768×32768 | block 32×1×1 | per launch: global load 4,611,686,018,427,387,904 B, store 4,611,686,018,427,387,904 B; param load ? B{{$}}
